      <Placemark>
        <name>Rooftop Bar Andaz Tokyo Toranomon Hills</name>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1798-F57C00-nodesc</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            139.7493926,35.6668835,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>APOLLO BAR GINZA</name>
        <description>Incredible whiskey selection, and a very gracious host. Don’t expect much English (you are in Japan, so you should not expect it), and like all small specialty bars, there is a small cover charge; however the host is gracious and we spent hours speaking about samurai films, whiskey, and music. Did I mention the whiskey selection is amazing?</description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1798-F57C00</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            139.7595177,35.6697749,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Sawanoi - Ozawa brewery</name>
        <description>Great spot for a quiet day in Ome. Easy walk from Sawai Station and right on the river, so you actually get scenery while you drink. The tastings are cheap and good, and you keep the little cup. Tours fill up fast and are only in Japanese, but the staff is helpful and the whole place is relaxed. If you’re already doing the valley or the river walk, stopping here is worth it.</description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1798-9C27B0</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            139.1934763,35.8047969,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
