      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Ide Sake Brewery</name>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1798-9C27B0-nodesc</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            138.7656011,35.5020647,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name><![CDATA[BAR Willow's]]></name>
        <description>Incredibly attentive bartender with clear, careful English and a real sense of hospitality. This has become a regular stop for me in Tokyo and I end up here multiple times every trip. Quiet, small, and easy to relax in, even though it sits above a row of louder bars. Cocktails are precise, the Moscow mule and martini in particular, and the light food works well if you stay for a few rounds. There is a table charge and you pay for hand–carved ice and mineral water, but the prices make sense for the level of service. If you want a calm bar where you are actually looked after, this is worth paying for.</description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1798-F57C00</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            139.7725963,35.7082581,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
