    <Folder>
      <name>Nature, Temples, Nakahechi Route; and Nakasendo Route</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Imado Shrine</name>
        <description><![CDATA[description: Quiet, a little out of the way, and worth the walk if you love cats or small neighborhood shrines. Imado is packed with maneki-neko imagery and ema for love and marriage, but it still feels like a local place rather than a tourist stop. The staff are kind, the atmosphere is relaxed, and on a good day you might even spot the resident white cat wandering through the grounds. I<br>説明: <br>nom: ]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1804-A52714</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="description">
            <value>Quiet, a little out of the way, and worth the walk if you love cats or small neighborhood shrines. Imado is packed with maneki-neko imagery and ema for love and marriage, but it still feels like a local place rather than a tourist stop. The staff are kind, the atmosphere is relaxed, and on a good day you might even spot the resident white cat wandering through the grounds. I</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="説明">
            <value/>
          </Data>
          <Data name="nom">
            <value/>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
