      <Placemark>
        <name>Murou Art Forest</name>
        <description><![CDATA[description: The installations are simple but they feel intentional, and the open space around them makes the whole park calm in a way most places in Kansai are not. The walk is easy, the air is clean, and the scenery around the hills is what stays with you more than the sculptures. There is no food inside and the facilities are older, so plan ahead, but if you like slow, quiet places where you can walk, read, or take photos without fighting for space, this is a good stop.<br>説明: <br>nom: ]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1720-0F9D58</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="description">
            <value>The installations are simple but they feel intentional, and the open space around them makes the whole park calm in a way most places in Kansai are not. The walk is easy, the air is clean, and the scenery around the hills is what stays with you more than the sculptures. There is no food inside and the facilities are older, so plan ahead, but if you like slow, quiet places where you can walk, read, or take photos without fighting for space, this is a good stop.</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="説明">
            <value/>
          </Data>
          <Data name="nom">
            <value/>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            136.0316225,34.5370822,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
